  "preamble": "Middle Chinese voiced stops lost their voicing in most varieties. In Mandarin they became aspirated in level-tone syllables and unaspirated in the others. In Hakka and Gan they became aspirated regardless of tone, while Wu and Old Xiang kept the voiced series. In Nyah Kur (Monic) former *b became aspirated pʰ with a low tone or breathy reflex (Proto-Monic *sa-bluuʔ 'betel' > tǝphùuʔ). In Western Armenian the Classical Armenian voiced stop բ /b/ became aspirated [pʰ], merging with փ (բան 'thing' [pʰɑn]), while Eastern Armenian keeps [b].",
